  "reason": "Inspected actual FSB comparisons, both obliques, neutral and grazing. Source-surface masks remove cloth from hands and skin from tunic. Albedo-only diagnostic ablation does not remove streaks: root cause remains in projected RGB, not inferred PBR relief. Atlas has >190 RGB texels on trousers while every owned source pixel is dark: source automatic mipmaps use a different footprint from non-mipmapped ownership masks. Also .2 de-light normalization brightens an already unlit flat-fill source (e.g. pants 36/58/85 to 57/91/134), differing from inferred palette continuation. Source depth sampling produces excessive self-occlusion. Reject; restore independent PBR maps, use consistent source sampling and source-appropriate upstream de-light, then rerender. Diagnostic-only material is explicitly barred from acceptance.",
